{"requirements":[{"id":"node1_nginx_http_6700","requirement":"Install Nginx on AlmaLinux node1 and successfully serve `/` over HTTP on TCP 6700.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Nginx was installed and configured on node1. Direct checks showed active service, IPv4/IPv6 listeners on 6700, and HTTP 200 with the node1 page before and after restart; the final cross-node check also succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7ed8a00367144349","cmd-b7cefcdb91d94b58","cmd-6aee557211584be7","cmd-fe9b7facb2204e56","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"node2_nginx_http_6700","requirement":"Install Nginx on AlmaLinux node2 and successfully serve `/` over HTTP on TCP 6700.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Nginx was installed and configured on node2. Direct checks showed active service, IPv4/IPv6 listeners on 6700, and HTTP 200 with the node2 page before and after restart; the final cross-node check also succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-44778c1c77694acd","cmd-4f58251390de424d","cmd-2e985c7181f64b58","cmd-fe9b7facb2204e56","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"node3_nginx_http_6700","requirement":"Install Nginx on Alpine node3 and successfully serve `/` over HTTP on TCP 6700.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Nginx was installed and enabled through OpenRC on node3. Direct checks showed the service started, IPv4/IPv6 listeners on 6700, and HTTP 200 with the node3 page before and after restart; the final cross-node check also succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2fe64ba030054e0f","cmd-9a2c14dcece44283","cmd-abd12e5231e940c3","cmd-fe9b7facb2204e56","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"node4_nginx_http_6700","requirement":"Install Nginx on Alpine node4 and successfully serve `/` over HTTP on TCP 6700.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Nginx was installed and enabled through OpenRC on node4. Direct checks showed the service started, IPv4/IPv6 listeners on 6700, and HTTP 200 with the node4 page before and after restart; the final cross-node check also succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f13d1082805340a5","cmd-907a825ef41c4749","cmd-b182a19f8e95421c","cmd-fe9b7facb2204e56","global:after_executor:node4:listening-sockets"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.8,"summary":"All task-related mutations had a clear role, and final package checks were healthy with no failed systemd units. The restart protocol was complete on all four nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot ID corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered Nginx service/content. Retained hygiene issues were: the packaged default virtual hosts unnecessarily exposed Nginx on TCP 80 on all four nodes in addition to required port 6700; this remained present after execution. Three small temporary evidence artifacts also remained: `/tmp/nginx-final-check` on node1 and `/tmp/benchmark-reboot-node3.log` and `/tmp/benchmark-reboot-node4.log`; these were not cleaned. No other unnecessary mutation is established by the trace—the failed Alpine configuration-path attempts and initial SELinux-blocked starts contributed directly to corrective implementation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7ed8a00367144349","cmd-44778c1c77694acd","cmd-2fe64ba030054e0f","cmd-f13d1082805340a5","cmd-fe9b7facb2204e56","cmd-d7a79f223e8c4ce0","cmd-0d324a6ba4494330","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node4:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node4:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The public task is fully satisfied: all four correctly identified operating systems have Nginx installed and return HTTP 200 for `/` over TCP 6700. Cross-node testing confirms network reachability, and the provider-wide restart protocol convincingly demonstrates persistence and recovery on every node. Hygiene is reduced by unnecessary retained port-80 exposure and three minor temporary files.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector cannot report failed OpenRC services on Alpine; however, direct executor checks demonstrated that Nginx was started and serving after restart on node3 and node4.","The final lifecycle snapshots confirm listeners and boot identities but do not independently issue HTTP requests; successful final HTTP behavior is supplied by the executor's direct cross-node matrix.","The contents and size of the retained Alpine reboot log files were not captured, although their creation and continued presence are directly shown."]}
